DIAG: remoteproc: take a coredump of the Q6 when it faults

Temporary, not for upstream.

The Q6 raises its fatal interrupt on every boot with no message, and SMEM
item 421 turns out not to exist at all, so there is nothing to read. A
coredump of its own memory is the way to find out what it thinks went
wrong -- and the machinery is already wired up: dump_conf is
RPROC_COREDUMP_ENABLED and a segment covers all 33 MiB of q6_region.

It has never produced anything because rproc_coredump() bails on
"ELF class is not set". rproc_alloc() leaves elf_class at ELFCLASSNONE,
and the only code that assigns it is rproc_elf_sanity_check(), installed
only for drivers that supply no .load op. qcom_q6v5_mpd supplies one, so
it is never set. The firmware images say ELFCLASS32 / EM_QDSP6.

Add SMEM to the dump as well, since a crash reason written to the WCSS
private partition lands there and nowhere the driver looks.

Do not move the dump ahead of rproc_stop(). Reading the Q6 window while
the Q6 is still running takes a synchronous external abort:

  Internal error: synchronous external abort: 0000000096000010 [#1] SMP
  Workqueue: rproc_recovery_wq rproc_crash_handler_work

so the shutdown has to happen first.

Signed-off-by: Hideo Sumi <hideo.sumi@mugops.com>
---
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_mpd.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_mpd.c
@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@
 #include <linux/io.h>
 #include <linux/iopoll.h>
 #include <linux/kernel.h>
+#include <linux/elf.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/of_address.h>
 #include <linux/of_device.h>
@@ -938,9 +939,24 @@
 
 	/* DBG: dump the whole Q6 region on crash so the firmware's own
 	 * error text can be recovered from it.
+	 *
+	 * rproc_coredump() refuses to run unless elf_class is set, and
+	 * nothing sets it here: rproc_alloc() leaves it ELFCLASSNONE and
+	 * only rproc_elf_sanity_check() ever assigns it, which is installed
+	 * only for drivers that supply no .load op. This driver has one, so
+	 * every crash so far has printed "ELF class is not set" and dumped
+	 * nothing. The firmware images are ELFCLASS32 / EM_QDSP6 -- their
+	 * headers start 7f 45 4c 46 01 with e_machine 0xa4.
 	 */
+	rproc->elf_class = ELFCLASS32;
+	rproc->elf_machine = 164;		/* EM_QDSP6 */
 	rproc_coredump_add_segment(rproc, wcss->mem_phys, wcss->mem_size);
 
+	/* SMEM too: a crash reason written to the WCSS private partition
+	 * lands here and nowhere the driver currently looks.
+	 */
+	rproc_coredump_add_segment(rproc, 0x4a800000, 0x100000);
+
 	wcss->num_clks = devm_clk_bulk_get_all(wcss->dev, &wcss->clks);
 	if (wcss->num_clks < 0)
 		return dev_err_probe(wcss->dev, wcss->num_clks,
